{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bea25feef7bcd916", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Self-Supervised Speech Representation Learning: A Review\narXiv: 2205.10643\nAuthors: Abdelrahman Mohamed, Hung-yi Lee, Lasse Borgholt, Jakob D. Havtorn, Joakim Edin, Christian Igel, Katrin Kirchhoff, Shang-Wen Li, Karen Livescu, Lars Maaløe, Tara N. Sainath, Shinji Watanabe\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Categorizes current speech self-supervised learning approaches into generative, contrastive, and predictive paradigms while highlighting their unique challenges.\n  2. Provides a comprehensive review of benchmark datasets, evaluation settings, and standardized benchmarks for assessing self-supervised speech representations.\n  3. Analyzes the information content, robustness, and transferability of learned representations, including the impact of training criteria and model size.\n  4. Surveys zero-resource speech technologies and textless NLP, demonstrating how self-supervised representations enable unsupervised ASR and language modeling.\n  5. Identifies key future research directions, including improving model efficiency, feature disentanglement, robustness, and the integration of text representation models.\n\nTags: SSL/生成式, SSL/对比式, SSL/预测式-离散, SSL/预测式-连续, SSL/多模态", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5fc23de6-1e28-4d30-8278-fbbec682d701", "uuid": "c7e0fc06-a38b-488c-a1ef-6e59e909e5ac", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T06:56:39.665Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Self-Supervised Speech Representation Learning: A Review\narXiv: 2205.10643\nAuthors: Abdelrahman Mohamed, Hung-yi Lee, Lasse Borgholt, Jakob D. Havtorn, Joakim Edin, Christian Igel, Katrin Kirchhoff, Shang-Wen Li, Karen Livescu, Lars Maaløe, Tara N. Sainath, Shinji Watanabe\nYear: 2022 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Categorizes current speech self-supervised learning approaches into generative, contrastive, and predictive paradigms while highlighting their unique challenges.\n  2. Provides a comprehensive review of benchmark datasets, evaluation settings, and standardized benchmarks for assessing self-supervised speech representations.\n  3. Analyzes the information content, robustness, and transferability of learned representations, including the impact of training criteria and model size.\n  4. Surveys zero-resource speech technologies and textless NLP, demonstrating how self-supervised representations enable unsupervised ASR and language modeling.\n  5. Identifies key future research directions, including improving model efficiency, feature disentanglement, robustness, and the integration of text representation models.\n\nTags: SSL/生成式, SSL/对比式, SSL/预测式-离散, SSL/预测式-连续, SSL/多模态", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
